tsrs-only: port of typescript-go's project/api.go `Session.APIUpdate`, which tsrs has not ported (its
update_snapshot_ref and merge_file_change_summary were dead code waiting for it). effect-tsgo's etsdiagnostics
(`--effect-cli-diagnostics`, crates/ets_etsdiagnostics) opens the requested project or file through it, as the Go
build does through the shim's `project.Session.APIUpdate`.

- tsrs_project::Session::api_update(ctx, api_file_changes, api_request) -> Result<Arc<Snapshot>, lsproto::Error>:
  Go's body (cancel the scheduled update, flush the pending changes, derive the snapshot with an extra caller
  reference, on an API error release it and still adopt the flushed host changes). As tsrs's
  SnapshotHost::clone_snapshot, a layered request file system takes precedence over `file_system`.
- The two `#[expect(dead_code)]` attributes that waited for this caller are removed.

